## Why This Is Asked
This probes ability to design privacy-aware, geo-distributed ML pipelines on GCP, balancing data residency, DP, drift and cost.

## Key Concepts
- Vertex AI training/serving (region-scoped)
- Vertex AI Feature Store (per-region stores)
- Dataflow for streaming ETL with DP transforms
- Pub/Sub for event ingestion
- Differential privacy, drift detection, automatic rollback, cost caps

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo DP transform sketch
function dpClipAndNoise(features, clipBound, epsilon) {
  Object.keys(features).forEach(k => {
    features[k] = Math.max(-clipBound, Math.min(clipBound, features[k]));
  });
  for (let k in features) { features[k] += laplace(1/epsilon); }
  return features;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-region data residency for training data across regions?
- How would you test canary rollouts and rollback safety at scale?
- How would you monitor DP utility vs. model accuracy in production?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes how a candidate designs a privacy-conscious, multi-tenant ML pipeline on GCP, balancing data governance, per-tenant isolation, cost, and operability.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation with per-tenant datasets and Feature Store
- PII de-identification in Dataflow
- Canary deployments and traffic shifting
- Drift detection and Explainable AI for governance
- Privacy logging and rollback mechanisms

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: shift partial traffic to canary on drift alert
function rollbackOnDrift(isDrift, canaryEndpoint, prodEndpoint){
  if(!isDrift) return;
  // gradually shift traffic back to prod
  setTraffic(canaryEndpoint, 0.0);
  setTraffic(prodEndpoint, 1.0);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding with data retention?
- How would you scale feature store lookups for thousands of tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-tenant inference with strict data residency, budgets, and auditable lineage in a real-world GCP setup.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation in Vertex AI Endpoints and Feature Store namespaces
- Routing logic with per-tenant budget and latency SLAs
- Data Catalog metadata tagging for lineage and governance
- Drift detection and rollback triggers per tenant

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing function
async function routeRequest(tenantId, req) {
  const budgetOk = checkBudget(tenantId);
  const latencyOk = checkLatency(tenantId);
  const endpoint = budgetOk && latencyOk ? getTenantEndpoint(tenantId) : getSharedEndpoint();
  return await predict(endpoint, req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-tenant quotas in Feature Store and endpoints?
- How would you simulate rollback scenarios and validate audit trails?
